  "name": "Stone Cross",
  "description": "Captures farewell as a whole way of life ending. A Ukrainian peasant spends his last night before emigrating to Canada saying goodbye, and carves himself a stone cross — the austere black-and-white twin of Shadows, from the same national school.\n\nIn 1890s Western Ukraine, Ivan Didukh, a proud and ripe Galician farmer, has decided to abandon his ancestral home to emigrate to Canada in search of a better life. His final hours are clouded by both internal and communal discord as his village convenes to ceremonially mark his departure. The celebrations that echo those of a funeral, forecast the imminent death of a man estranged from his motherland, and of an antiquated way of life on the cusp of obsoletion.",
